1. Update: Important Assessment Principle for Best-of-Breed Selection
Replace Existing Ranking Principle

Current Order

Expected Best-of-Design Attributes
Extent of Coverage

Replace With

The ranking must be driven primarily by the following criteria in order of importance:

Alignment to the Control Objective
Alignment to the Expected Control Nature
Expected Best-of-Design Attributes
Extent of Coverage
Additional Guidance

A control that more directly performs the control activity contemplated by the control objective should generally rank above controls that primarily provide:

Monitoring
Investigation
Escalation
Governance
Reporting
Assurance

